%S A399830 1,2,2,2,2,4,2,4,2,4,2,4,2,4,4,5,2,4,2,4,4,4,2,8,2,4,4,4,2,8,2,6,4,4,
%T A399830 4,4,2,4,4,8,2,8,2,4,4,4,2,10,2,4,4,4,2,8,4,8,4,4,2,8,2,4,4,6,4,8,2,4,
%U A399830 4,8,2,8,2,4,4,4,4,8,2,10,5,4,2,8,4,4,4,8,2,8
%N A399830 The number of divisors d of n such that gcud(d, n/d) is a square, where gcud is the greatest common unitary divisor.
%C A399830 The sum of these divisors is A399836(n).
%H A399830 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A399830/b399830.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A399830 Multiplicative with a(p^e) = e if e == 2 (mod 4), and e + 1 otherwise.
%F A399830 Dirichlet g.f.: zeta(s) * zeta(4*s) * Product_{p prime} (1 + 1/p^s + 2/p^(3*s)).
%t A399830 f[p_, e_] := If[Mod[e, 4] == 2, e, e + 1]; a[1] = 1; a[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 100]
%o A399830 (PARI) a(n) = vecprod(apply(x -> if(x % 4 == 2, x, x+1), factor(n)[, 2]));
%Y A399830 Cf. A000290, A077610, A165430, A225174, A384244.
%Y A399830 Cf. A365171 (analogous with gcd), A399836.
%Y A399830 The number of divisors d of n such that gcud(d, n/d) is: A286324 (1), A399828 (squarefree), A399829 (powerful), this sequence (square), A399831 (exponentially odd), A399832 (odd), A399833 (power of 2).
%K A399830 nonn,mult,easy,new
%O A399830 1,2
